r economic policies. ([source](https://www.ft.com/content/07cdbe96-33f8-45bd-a777-4aa8f0ca3ab7?utm_source=openai))  4. **Tariffs Impacting Indian Economy**:    - India's economy is under strain following the imposition of near-50% tariffs on its exports to the U.S. This move, amidst rising geopolitical tensions, is predicted to lower India’s GDP growth significantly, affecting sectors like textiles and jewelry which are heavily reliant on exports. ([source](https://www.reuters.com/world/india/india-file-trump-modi-standoff-tests-indias-economy-2025-08-13/?utm_source=openai))  5. **Australian Interest Rate Predictions**:    - The Reserve Bank of Australia (RBA) is anticipated to cut rates by 25 basis points in its upcoming meeting, responding to a declining inflation rate that slipped to 2.1% in Q2. This indicates a robust effort to stimulate economic activity in light of global uncertainties. ([source](https://www.ig.com/en/news-and-trade-ideas/weekly-market-navigator--11-aug-2025-250811?utm_source=openai))  ### Corporate Developments: Apple Inc.  1. **Massive U.S. Investment Commitment**:    - Apple has announced a substantial $100 billion commitment to increasing its U.S. manufacturing footprint, bringing its total investment to $600 billion over four years. This move is seen as a strategic response to the U.S. tariffs and is likely to strengthen Apple’s domestic production capabilities, particularly as it seeks to mitigate tariff liabilities on its products. ([source](https://www.cbsnews.com/news/apple-us-manufacturing-commitment-august-2025/?utm_source=openai))  2. **AI and Technological Advances**:    - Apple is set to enhance its Siri capabilities with an upcoming AI voice control feature that could significantly change user interaction with iPhones. The focus will also shift towards integrating OpenAI's GPT-5 into Apple’s platforms, showcasing a comeback in their AI strategy which is critical for staying competitive in the technology space. ([source]())  3. *